nt=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"209\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Euclid.jpg/500px-Euclid.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"806\" data-file-height=\"675\" /></a></span><div class=\"infobox-caption\"><a href=\"/wiki/Euclid\" title=\"Euclid\">Euclid</a> (holding <a href=\"/wiki/Calipers\" title=\"Calipers\">calipers</a>), Greek mathematician, known as the \"Father of Geometry\"</div></td></tr><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-header\">Occupation</th></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0;\">Occupation type</div></th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><a href=\"/wiki/Academy\" title=\"Academy\">Academic</a></td></tr><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-header\">Description</th></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\">Competencies</th><td class=\"infobox-data\">Mathematics, <a href=\"/wiki/Analytical_skill\" title=\"Analytical skill\">analytical skills</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Critical_thinking\" title=\"Critical thinking\">critical thinking</a> skills</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0;\">Education required</div></th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><a href=\"/wiki/Doctoral_degree\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Doctoral degree\">Doctoral degree</a>, occasionally master's degree</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0;\">Fields of<br />employment</div></th><td class=\"infobox-data\">universities, <br />private corporations, <br />financial industry, <br />government</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0;\">Related jobs</div></th><td class=\"infobox-data\">statistician, <a href=\"/wiki/Actuary\" title=\"Actuary\">actuary</a></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>A <b>mathematician</b> is someone who uses an extensive knowledge of <a href=\"/wiki/Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a> in their work, typically to solve <a href=\"/wiki/Mathematical_problem\" title=\"Mathematical problem\">mathematical problems</a>. Mathematicians are concerned with numbers, data, <a href=\"/wiki/Quantity\" title=\"Quantity\">quantity</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Mathematical_structure\" title=\"Mathematical structure\">structure</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Space\" title=\"Space\">space</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Mathematical_model\" title=\"Mathematical model\">models</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Mathematics#Calculus_and_analysis\" title=\"Mathematics\">change</a>.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐lk9p5\nCached time: 20260918181013\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, prevent‐selective‐update]\nCPU time usage: 0.062 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.112 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 403/1000000\nRevision size: 1016/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 6601/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1578/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 8/100\nExpensive parser function count: 3/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1425/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.035/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1807458/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 1/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   99.157      1 -total\n 45.63%   45.247      1 Template:Short_description\n 34.74%   34.447      1 Template:Infobox_Occupation\n 31.99%   31.722      1 Template:Infobox\n 28.27%   28.028      2 Template:Pagetype\n 19.50%   19.335      1 Template:Pp\n 10.06%    9.974      3 Template:Main_other\n  9.09%    9.009      1 Template:SDcat\n  1.51%    1.493      4 Template:Longitem\n  1.27%    1.262      1 Templat